{%- comment -%}
  Emits the head tags a generated PLP needs that Shopify does not provide for
  blog articles.

  hreflang is the reason this block exists. Locale variants of a PLP have to
  reference each other with `<link rel="alternate" hreflang>` in the document
  head, and a non-reciprocal or absent annotation is simply discarded by
  search engines. There is no way to put a head tag there from an article
  body, and Shopify emits hreflang only for its own Markets URLs.

  Deliberately absent: `<link rel="canonical">`. Every Theme Store theme
  already emits a self-referencing canonical for an article and an app
  extension cannot remove it, so adding a second one naming a different URL is
  a mixed signal search engines may discard entirely. Under the app's canonical
  policy every market page is canonical for itself, so the theme's tag is
  already the right one; locale variants are related by the hreflang above,
  never by consolidation. The single exception — two near-duplicate pages in
  the *same* market — is recorded in sitemap-ai.xml, and emitting it as a head
  tag needs template-based publishing. See the README.

  The payload is written by the app on publish, to the storefront-readable
  metafield wp_plp.seo. `article` is nil outside article templates, so `plp`
  is nil there and nothing is emitted.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign plp = article.metafields.wp_plp.seo.value
-%}

{%- if plp -%}
  {%- for alternate in plp.hreflang -%}
    {%- if alternate.locale and alternate.url -%}
      <link rel="alternate" hreflang="{{ alternate.locale }}" href="{{ alternate.url }}">
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Belt and braces alongside the seo.hidden metafield the app also sets. A
    page held for review never reaches the storefront at all, so this should
    never fire; if it does, something upstream is wrong and the page must not
    be indexed while it is.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if plp.noindex -%}
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow">
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "PLP SEO tags",
  "target": "head",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
